.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "has-flag [![Build Status](https://travis-ci.org/sindresorhus/has-flag.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.org/sindresorhus/has-flag)"
.PP
.RS 4
Check if \fR\fRargv\fP\fP has a specific flag 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Correctly stops looking after an \fR--\fP argument terminator\&.

.PP
.PP

.PP
 \fB \fRGet professional support for this package with a Tidelift subscription\fP \fP 
.br
 \*< Tidelift helps make open source sustainable for maintainers while giving companies
.br
assurances about security, maintenance, and licensing for their dependencies\&. \*>  

.PP
.PP
.SH "Install"
.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install has\-flag
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
// foo\&.js
const hasFlag = require('has\-flag');

hasFlag('unicorn');
//=> true

hasFlag('\-\-unicorn');
//=> true

hasFlag('f');
//=> true

hasFlag('\-f');
//=> true

hasFlag('foo=bar');
//=> true

hasFlag('foo');
//=> false

hasFlag('rainbow');
//=> false
.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
$ node foo\&.js \-f \-\-unicorn \-\-foo=bar \-\- \-\-rainbow
.fi
.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
.SS "hasFlag(flag, [argv])"
Returns a boolean for whether the flag exists\&.
.SS "flag"
Type: \fRstring\fP

.PP
CLI flag to look for\&. The \fR--\fP prefix is optional\&.
.SS "argv"
Type: \fRstring[]\fP
.br
 Default: \fRprocess\&.argv\fP

.PP
CLI arguments\&.
